hostlibs/<platform>/ - libraries built against the DEVICE's own glibc, loaded by
apkenv with the real dlopen() and bridged into the bionic namespace by
compat/hostlib.c.

Do NOT put these in libs/<platform>/. That directory is APKENV_LOCAL_BIONIC_PATH,
the search path of apkenv's *bionic* linker, and packaging/build-ipk.sh copies
*.so out of it into the jail's bionic lib dir. These are glibc objects; they must
never be handed to the bionic linker.

  webos/libmono-webos.so   Unity's Mono 2.6.5 runtime (Unity-Technologies/mono
                           @ unity3.5, commit 64c3378a), built by
                           tools/build-mono-webos.sh. Stands in for the bionic
                           libmono.so inside templerun2_1.2.1.apk, whose export
                           set it matches exactly (910 symbols, zero diff).

  unity42/libmono-unity42.so
                           Unity's Mono 2.6.5 runtime at Unity 4.2
                           (Unity-Technologies/mono @ unity-4.2, commit ac09c9bb),
                           built by `tools/build-mono-webos.sh unity4.2`. Stands in
                           for the bionic libmono.so of RoboCop 3.0.6 (Unity 4.2.2f1),
                           whose export set it matches exactly (931 symbols). Kept in
                           its own directory so packaging a Unity 3.5/4.0 game does
                           not ship it: pass HOSTLIBS=hostlibs/unity42 to
                           packaging/build-ipk.sh, which installs it as
                           hostlibs/webos/libmono-unity42.so in the app.

LICENSE
  Both runtimes are built, unmodified apart from tools/mono-webos.patch, from
  Unity's public fork of Mono (https://github.com/Unity-Technologies/mono). The
  Mono runtime (libmono) is licensed under the GNU LGPL v2; the corresponding
  source is that repository at the commits above plus tools/mono-webos.patch,
  and tools/build-mono-webos.sh rebuilds each library from it.
